## FIREBASE ARCHITECTURE

### Single Firebase Project — Subcollection-based Isolation

```
Firestore Structure:

institutes/                              ← top-level collection
  {instituteId}/                         ← one doc per institute
    config (document):
      institute_id: string
      name: string                       ← "MAAC Raipur"
      reg_prefix: string                 ← "MAAC" → generates MAAC-2026-27-0001
      email: string
      phone: string
      city: string
      address: string
      logo_url: string (optional)
      admin_email: string                ← linked Firebase Auth user
      status: "active" | "suspended" | "trial"
      plan: "basic" | "standard" | "pro"
      created_date: string
      emailjs_service_id: string         ← per-institute EmailJS config
      emailjs_template_admission: string
      emailjs_template_payment: string
      emailjs_public_key: string
      whatsapp_number: string (optional)
      features: {
        finance_module: boolean
        fee_reminders: boolean
        birthday_greetings: boolean
        certificate_verify: boolean
        import_leads: boolean
        backup_restore: boolean
      }

    students/                            ← subcollection
      {studentId}: Student document

    payments/                            ← subcollection
      {paymentId}: Payment document

    expenses/                            ← subcollection
      {expenseId}: Expense document

    courses/                             ← subcollection
      {courseId}: CourseOption document

    batches/                             ← subcollection
      {batchId}: BatchOption document

    counters/                            ← subcollection
      {fyKey}: { seq: number }           ← for serial reg number generation
```

### Firebase Auth
- Each institute admin is a Firebase Auth user
- On login, app reads `institutes` collection to find doc where `config.admin_email == user.email`
- Super Admin is identified by: `user.email === import.meta.env.VITE_SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL`
- No self-registration allowed anywhere — all accounts created by Super Admin only

### Firestore Security Rules
```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }

    match /institutes/{instituteId} {
      // Super admin can read all
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.token.email == "SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL_PLACEHOLDER";

      // Institute admin can only read their own config
      allow read: if request.auth != null;

      match /students/{studentId} {
        allow read, write: if request.auth != null;
      }
      match /payments/{paymentId} {
        allow read, write: if request.auth != null;
      }
      match /expenses/{expenseId} {
        allow read, write: if request.auth != null;
      }
      match /courses/{courseId} {
        allow read, write: if request.auth != null;
      }
      match /batches/{batchId} {
        allow read, write: if request.auth != null;
      }
      match /counters/{counterId} {
        allow read, write: if request.auth != null;
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Note: Data isolation is enforced in app logic — each institute user only queries their own instituteId path.

